{title: Lift Me High}
{subtitle: Psalms 69:30–31}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Em] | [Em] | [C] | [C] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]I am afflicted in my pain
[C]My spirit feels the weight
[D]But your salvation O God
Will lift me high [Em]today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [C]praise the name [D]of God with [Em]song
I will [C]magnify him [D]with thanks[Em]giving
This will [C]please the LORD [D]more than an [G]ox
More than a [D]bull with horns and [Em]hooves
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The humble will see it and be glad
[C]You who seek God let your hearts revive
For [D]the LORD hears the needy truly
And does [Em]not despise his own in chains
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C]Lift me high out of [D]my pain
[Em]Your praise is the sweet[G]est sound
[C]My soul will rejoice in [D]your name
In this [Bm]holy and sacred ground
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Lift me [C]high [D][Em]with your [C][D][Em]song
Magnify [C][D]him with [D]thanksgiving [Em]
{end_of_verse}
